        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹೊಗಳು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೊಗಳು — hogaḷu — \"to praise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಶಿಕ್ಷಕರು ನನ್ನ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳಿದರು. śikṣakaru nanna katheyannu hogaḷidaru. The teacher praised my story."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಹೊಗಳಿದೆ, hogaḷide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is praised takes -ಅನ್ನು. ಹೊಗಳಿಕೆ is praise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೊಗಳು (hogaḷu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4235 lists an older Kannada form in p-, \"to praise; praise, renown\". Old p- became h- in the modern language."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
